>  <SOURCE_REFERENCES>
["https://doi.org/10.1002/wcms.1606","https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jctc.8b01176","https://doi.org/10.1021/om300159r","https://github.com/jensengroup/xyz2mol_tm/blob/db2734b084045ef895528c7a3d5040d38da23983/SMILES_csvs/csd_smiles.csv","https://github.com/jensengroup/xyz2mol_tm/blob/db2734b084045ef895528c7a3d5040d38da23983/SMILES_csvs/tmqmg_smiles.csv","https://github.com/uiocompcat/tmQMg/tree/e1dc9887b8f20a217a1db6ca972d726bcbaab45b","https://www.crystallography.net/cod/4078264.cif"]

>  <SELECTION_REASON>
Single-point calculation on the original coordinates and ligand-by-ligand Lewis review. In the original XYZ, Cl forms a direct N–Cl bond to the heterocyclic nitrogen. Retain three separate carbonyls, Write each as C⁻≡O⁺, Draw the conjugated sulfur-containing skeleton using its short C–C multiple bonds and its N–N and C–S connectivity. A monoanionic ligand balances Re(I). Localized 10 aromatic-ring bonds using WBOs and original bond lengths. Use the supplied Lewis representation for scoring; Independent evidence for the complete graph is limited.

