>  <SELECTION_REASON>
Manually reviewed Lewis representation. Acetate and a sulfonamide anion balance Zn(II). The imine N is neutral, Benzimidazole retains one N–H. The crystal deposition confirms each of these groups. Localized 28 aromatic-ring bonds using WBOs and original bond lengths. The original paper or deposition identifies the ligands, Checked against the supplied coordinates site by site. The atom order and coordinates of all 63 atoms agree between XYZ and SDF. Lengths of 65 nonmetal covalent bonds: 65 within range, 0 outside range and 0 with sparse controls. Use the supplied Lewis representation for scoring; Independent evidence for the complete graph is limited.

